{{!-- "This season" — the named moments within it, and what fires at each.

      The wheel turning is not the only thing that happens in a season. "When the autumn harvest is
      complete" fires DURING autumn, and the sheet has no way to know when: no amount of watching the
      calendar tells it the harvest came in or that anyone led the hunt. So this is an offer the table
      takes up, not a schedule the sheet runs — one panel per moment, each with its own statement and
      its own Apply, each owed again when its season next comes round.

      Only moments something built actually fires at are here. An empty panel headed "The autumn
      harvest" would read as a thing left undone.

      Params: turnover (TurnoverSnapshot). --}}
<section class="steading-moments steading-block">

	{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.momentsTitle")
	    note=(localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.momentsHint")}}

	{{#each turnover.moments}}
		<article class="steading-moment{{#if applied}} is-applied{{/if}}" data-moment="{{key}}">

			<h4 class="steading-moment-title">
				{{localize labelKey}}
				{{#if applied}}
					{{!-- Said rather than shown by absence: six people share this document, and the one
					      who was not here when it was pressed has no other way to learn it happened. --}}
					<span class="steading-moment-state">{{localize "stonetop.steading.effects.momentApplied"}}</span>
				{{/if}}
			</h4>

			{{> "stonetop.steading-statement" statement=statement showAdvisory=true
			    showSource=true showDelta=true
			    applyAllAction="applyMoment" applyAllSlug=key
			    applyAllLabel="stonetop.steading.effects.applyMoment"}}

		</article>
	{{/each}}

</section>
